# Fundamentals

Core concepts that form the base of data engineering.

## Topics

- Data Engineering  
  Building systems to collect, process, and store data for analytics.  
  Example: Moving sales data from source systems to a data lake for reporting.  
  Real-life: Companies use data engineering to prepare data for dashboards.

- Structured, Semi-structured, Unstructured Data  
  Different formats of data based on schema flexibility.  
  Example: Tables (structured), JSON (semi), images (unstructured).  
  Real-life: Logs usually come as JSON, while transactions are tables.

- ETL vs ELT  
  ETL transforms data before loading; ELT transforms after loading.  
  Example: Cleaning data in Spark before storing vs after storing in Synapse.  
  Real-life: ELT is common with cloud data warehouses.

- Batch vs Streaming  
  Batch processes data in chunks; streaming processes data continuously.  
  Example: Daily sales batch vs live clickstream data.  
  Real-life: Banking reports use batch, IoT systems use streaming.

- OLTP vs OLAP  
  OLTP handles transactions; OLAP handles analysis.  
  Example: Order placement vs sales summary report.  
  Real-life: Application DB vs reporting system.

- Data Warehouse vs Data Lake  
  Warehouse stores structured data; lake stores all data types.  
  Example: Synapse vs ADLS.  
  Real-life: Raw data lands in lake, reports read from warehouse.
